      "notes": [
        "**The місцевий never stands alone.** It's the only case that **must** come after a preposition: в, у, на, при, по. You'll never see *школі* without *в* or *у* in front of it. That's why it's the easiest of the seven cases to recognize.",
        "**The ending is almost always -і.** *Київ* → *у Києві*, *школа* → *у школі*, *стіл* → *на столі*, *кімната* → *у кімнаті*, *робота* → *на роботі*. Stick on **-і**, put a preposition in front, and you're right nine times out of ten.",
        "**The rest end in -у, and they're certain masculine nouns.** *Банк* → *у банку*, *гуртожиток* → *у гуртожитку*, *ринок* → *на ринку*, *сад* → *у саду*. There's no tidy rule; you pick these up through use, and there aren't many.",
        "**Foreign words ending in -о, -е, -у don't change at all.** *Кафе*, *метро*, *таксі*, *пальто* — same form in every case. A small gift that comes in handy fairly often.",
        "**В for things with walls, на for surfaces — but not always.** The big rule: *в квартирі*, *в кімнаті*, *в школі* (enclosed spaces) versus *на столі*, *на вулиці* (surfaces or open spaces). ⚠️ But there's a group to memorize: **на роботі**, **на вокзалі**, **на пошті**, **на заводі**, **на ринку**, **на метро** — all take *на* even though they're clearly indoors.",
        "**Neighborhoods and districts almost always take на.** *На Подолі*, *на Лівому березі*, *на Оболоні*. If you're unsure about a district name, *на* is a safer bet than *в*.",
        "**Жити is a first-pattern verb with a changing stem.** The dictionary form is *жити*, but the stem becomes **жив-**: *я живу*, *ти живеш*, *він живе*. This group of verbs is small, but it's full of high-frequency words — exactly the ones you'll say most."
      ],
